   "text": {
    "L1": "Animals do not all take in food in the same way.",
    "L2": "A cow grinds grass, a mosquito sucks liquid, and a snake swallows prey whole.",
    "L3": "An amoeba pushes out pseudopodia and surrounds tiny food particles.",
    "L4": "The food is trapped in a food vacuole, where digestive juices break it down.",
    "L5": "A cow swallows grass quickly and stores it in the rumen, the first stomach chamber.",
    "L6": "Microbes in the rumen partly break down cellulose, and lumps of cud later return to the mouth.",
    "L7": "The cow chews the cud again before digestion and absorption are completed.",
    "L8": "So the structures differ, but animals take in food, break it down, absorb it, and remove waste."
   },
